  "commentary_text": "In the previous example, a 7-stage ring oscillator is used as a noise source and only a single-CMOS inverter-amplifier as receiver. This has been extended to a 220-Kgates telecom chip as a noise source and a WLAN modem as receiver. The bonding wires are 6 nH. Both the peak-to-peak and the RMS noise are shown (on the left). The largest peak around 75 MHz can also be found by simulation. Accurate values have been introduced for all parasitic resistances and capacitances. There is a fairly linear relation between the noise and the supply voltage. This is a result of the increased current injection in the substrate, which increases linearly with the supply voltage. It is also found that as a great deal of noise is generated by the Input/Output buffers as by the digital gates themselves!",
  "schema_version": "1.0",
